Patch 47. After patch 45 (and 46, which touches other files).

On Android the host app is a shared library that SDLActivity loads, so its exported functions
could be preempted and every call it made to a function it defines itself went through the
PLT (on Torchlight, all 386,595 direct calls between guest functions). rexglue_configure_target
now links Android shared-library targets with -Wl,-Bsymbolic-functions, which binds those calls
inside the library. Only the link changes; the objects are the same.

What keeps its behaviour: a strong definition overriding a weak one in the same link (a hook
over a generated function) is chosen by the static linker before binding, so calls still reach
the hook; data keeps its usual binding (only functions are bound); calls into the app from other
libraries (SDL's dlsym of SDL_main) and the app's calls into librexruntime, libc and the GPU
plugins still go through their PLT entries. What changes besides the PLT: a definition in
another loaded object (a separate library, an LD_PRELOAD) no longer replaces one of the app's
functions for the app's own calls, so hooks have to be in the app's link, as the codegen's are.
Executables and other platforms are untouched: the option is added only when ANDROID is set and
the target is a SHARED_LIBRARY (ld64 has no such option either).

Test: a minimal project through rexglue_configure_target, configured for Android (NDK r30,
arm64-v8a) and for Linux: only the Android shared library links with the option. Torchlight's
desktop Linux build (Release) configured with and without the patch: all 619 build commands,
the game's link included, are identical. Torchlight's libtorchlight.so (POCO X7, Release,
2026-10-21): no branch to a guest sub_*@plt with it (391,037 without, tail calls included), and
no generated code reaches a hooked function past its hook (202 hooked); Torchlight checks both
on every Android link (tools/android/check_guest_call_binding.py). The combat bench, runs
alternated without and with it (P S S P, thermal status 0, CPU 34-39 C), mean guest frame time:
at rest 15.15 and 14.82 ms without, 13.99 and 13.69 ms with (-7.6 %, both runs with it below both
without); in a fight 29.46 and 26.39 ms without, 25.84 and 25.90 ms with (-7.4 %, but the two
runs without it differ by 10 %); guest frames over 33 ms in the fight 167 and 83 without, 60 and
44 with. The presented frame time in the fight did not change (36.5-39.4 ms either way):
presentation there is bound by the GPU.

diff --git a/cmake/rexglue_helpers.cmake b/cmake/rexglue_helpers.cmake
index 41e6dce..67e8f4b 100644
--- a/cmake/rexglue_helpers.cmake
+++ b/cmake/rexglue_helpers.cmake
@@ -101,6 +101,20 @@ function(rexglue_configure_target target_name)
 
     rexglue_apply_target_settings(${target_name})
 
+    # On Android the host app is a shared library (SDLActivity loads it), so every call it made to
+    # a function it defines itself, guest functions included, went through the PLT: its exported
+    # functions could be preempted. Bind those calls inside the library. A strong definition that
+    # overrides a weak one in the same link (a hook over a generated function) is chosen by the
+    # static linker first, so it still wins. Hooks must therefore be in the app's own link: a
+    # definition in another loaded library no longer replaces one of the app's functions for the
+    # app's calls. Data keeps its usual binding, and other libraries' calls into the app (SDL's
+    # dlsym of SDL_main) are unchanged.
+    get_target_property(_rexglue_target_type ${target_name} TYPE)
+    if(ANDROID AND _rexglue_target_type STREQUAL "SHARED_LIBRARY")
+        target_link_options(${target_name} PRIVATE -Wl,-Bsymbolic-functions)
+    endif()
+    unset(_rexglue_target_type)
+
     if(WIN32)
         # Stage runtime DLLs (rexruntime, TracyClient, etc.) next to the host
         # binary on every link. copy_if_different is a no-op when up to date.
